      "id": "MEM-1791548914308-d3af",
      "key": "turn_1",
      "value": {
        "thought": "The clues describe the late Kenyan author, scholar, and journalist Ken Walibora (Ken Walibora Waliaula). He tragically passed away following a road accident in Nairobi in April 2020. As a child, he aspired to be a police officer before pursuing education and writing. From 2018 until his death in 2020, he served as a lecturer and director at Riara University (a private university in Kenya). In 2018, in an interview with the Daily Nation, he noted that he writes stories that have 'no sell-by date'. In 2017, his novel 'Chozi la Heri' was selected by Kenya's Ministry of Education/KICD as a compulsory set book for secondary schools. Prior to his media and academic career, Walibora served as a probation officer at the Ministry of Home Affairs from 1988 to 1996.",
